      "package": "rea-dsh-plugin",
      "pluginDir": "rea-plugin-build/rea-dsh-plugin",
      "kind": "npm",
      "mode": "rebuild",
      "source": "rea-agents",
      "upstream": {
        "skillsRoot": "skills"
      },
      "recipe": "rea",
      "expectedSkills": [
        "reverse-engineer-anything",
        "rea-dsh"
      ],
      "manualSkills": [
        "rea-dsh"
      ],
      "license": "MIT",
      "notes": "Upstream publishes its agent skill inside the rea-agents npm package under skills/; the bundle vendors that published copy, and optionalDependencies['rea-agents'] pins the release it came from (the plugin's own 0.1.x line is unrelated to rea-agents 6.x, so the pin -- not the plugin version -- is the comparison baseline). The repository's .agents/skills/ holds a source-shaped copy whose links are repository-relative; it is never the upstream here. The 'Connect only when needed' section is replaced with the DSH wording in recipes/overlays/rea/, and rea-dsh is this plugin's own skill with no upstream counterpart: it is listed in both expectedSkills (it ships in the bundle) and manualSkills (the recipe carries the installed copy over unchanged instead of rebuilding it), the same shape vercel-skills-dsh uses for skills-cli."
    }
,
